{"name":"Cornmeal","hex":"#ffd691","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cornmeal","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Dried corn (maize) milled (ground) to a meal, especially a coarse one.","Any cereal grain meal or flour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cornmeal"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cornmeal","blocks":[{"text":"Cornmeal is a meal ground from dried maize. It is a common staple food and is ground to coarse, medium, and fine consistencies, but it is not as fine as wheat flour can be. In Mexico and Louisiana, very finely ground cornmeal is referred to as corn flour. When fine cornmeal is made from maize that has been soaked in an alkaline solution, e.g., limewater, it is called masa harina, which is used for making arepas, tamales, and tortillas. Boiled cornmeal is called polenta in Italy and is also a traditional dish and bread substitute in Romania."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Polenta_uncooked.jpg/330px-Polenta_uncooked.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cornmeal"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Nsima_Relishes.JPG/500px-Nsima_Relishes.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Nsima_Relishes.JPG/500px-Nsima_Relishes.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Southern Africa's nshima cornmeal (top right corner), served with three relishes.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANsima_Relishes.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Dunkin-Donuts-Corn-Muffin.jpg/500px-Dunkin-Donuts-Corn-Muffin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Dunkin-Donuts-Corn-Muffin.jpg/1280px-Dunkin-Donuts-Corn-Muffin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Dunkin-Donuts-Corn-Muffin.jpg/500px-Dunkin-Donuts-Corn-Muffin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A corn muffin from Dunkin' Donuts","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADunkin-Donuts-Corn-Muffin.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Mingus-mill-interior1.jpg/330px-Mingus-mill-interior1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Mingus-mill-interior1.jpg/330px-Mingus-mill-interior1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Grindstones inside Mingus Mill, in the Great Smoky Mountains of North Carolina. Corn is placed in a hopper (top right) which slowly feeds it into the grindstone (center). The grindstone grinds the corn into cornmeal, and empties it into a bucket (lower left). The grindstones are turned by the mill's water-powered turbine.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMingus-mill-interior1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Bugas_mais_%28Visayan_white_corn_grits%29%2C_Philippines_03.jpg/500px-Bugas_mais_%28Visayan_white_corn_grits%29%2C_Philippines_03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Bugas_mais_%28Visayan_white_corn_grits%29%2C_Philippines_03.jpg/1280px-Bugas_mais_%28Visayan_white_corn_grits%29%2C_Philippines_03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Bugas_mais_%28Visayan_white_corn_grits%29%2C_Philippines_03.jpg/500px-Bugas_mais_%28Visayan_white_corn_grits%29%2C_Philippines_03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_conten